= keep
- b92bf4672f The Truffle migration plan: replace jast2bc, phase by phase

= Truffle migration: Phases 1-4 recorded; a BEGIN block per 16 packages
Final conclusions of the four phases. Phase 1: the Bytecode DSL skeleton
runs, 34.0% of CORE.c's blocks encode, the calling convention is the
whole game. Phase 2: runtime-compiled blocks run on the engine behind
NQP_CODE_RUN=1 at t/01-sanity and t/02-rakudo parity, cold -e at parity,
the warm int loop ahead. Phase 3: loops with handlers, handle and
continuations on-engine at S04+S17 parity. Phase 4: engine programs bake
into jars (string road, lz4 sidecar for CORE.c) behind NQP_CODE_PRECOMP=1;
the engine build is the only build and docs/jvm-spectest-known-failing.txt
is what future runs diff against. The RakuAST gen emits one BEGIN block
per 16 packages (the single mainline OOM'd a 14GB compile); AGENTS.md
records that a heap OOM is a symptom, and how to cage a heavy build.
- 72cea5650a Truffle migration: Phase 1 done -- skeleton live, coverage measured
- 73b1c57373 Docs: follow the Qt* -> Nqp*/TruffleEncoder/NQP_CODE_* rename
- bde45636a4 Truffle migration: Phase 2 landed, gates recorded
- 9c9d6f2f3d RakuAST gen: one BEGIN block per 16 packages, not one for the tree
- 3417a2b0be Truffle migration: Phase 3 complete -- control flow and resume on-engine
- d81301a1a9 Truffle migration: Phase 4 complete -- precompiled modules and the setting on-engine

= Eval server: refuse over-budget starts, cage the JVM; .DELETE_ON_ERROR
rakudo-eval-server does the memory arithmetic itself (its ceiling plus
every live server's headroom against MemAvailable, exit 75 when it does
not fit) and runs the JVM under systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax.
dice-spectest.raku, the spot-check gate, passes --heap, surfaces a
refusal, cleans up best-effort, and honours never-run.txt for the steady
set too. The Makefile templates set .DELETE_ON_ERROR so a failed recipe
leaves no fresh-looking partial target.
